          "en": "Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court on Issues Concerning the Application of Relevant Laws in the Trial of Cases of Disputes over Export Credit Insurance Contracts was adopted at the 1,575th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 15 April 2013. It is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 8 May 2013.\n2 May 2013\nSupreme People's Court\nReply on Issues Concerning the Application of Relevant Laws in the\nTrial of Cases of Disputes over Export Credit Insurance Contracts\nFa Shi No. 13 [2013]\n(Adopted at the 1,575th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 15 April 2013; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 2 May 2013; coming into force on 8 May 2013)\nTo the Higher People's Court of Guangdong Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court on issues concerning the application of law to export credit insurance contracts (Yue Gao Fa No. 442 [2012]) has been received. After study, the following reply is given:\nThe Insurance Law does not expressly provide for the application of law to export credit insurance contracts. In view of the special nature of export credit insurance, a people's court trying a case of dispute over an export credit insurance contract may apply the relevant provisions of the Insurance Law by reference; where the export credit insurance contract provides otherwise, those provisions shall prevail."
